      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi. The use case here is a bit different. The actual issue is that once a configuration is added to the system using AddObject, it persists across reboots. The same configuration reappears on D-Bus after a BMC reboot or an AC power cycle.\n\nIn some cases, however, the configuration added through this method may no longer be valid after a reboot. In my case, the I2C bus number changed after the reboot, making the stored configuration invalid.\n\nAs a workaround for this behavior of AddObject, we proposed an API that adds the configuration at runtime without storing it permanently.",
